      "worked": "In triangles $ACP$ and $BCP$, use cosine = adjacent/hypotenuse.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos\\alpha&=\\frac{x}{b}\\\\x&=b\\cos\\alpha\\\\\\cos\\beta&=\\frac{y}{a}\\\\y&=a\\cos\\beta\\\\AB&=x+y\\\\AB&=a\\cos\\beta+b\\cos\\alpha\\end{align*}$$",
